law.text:
		The Small Business Environmental Compliance Advisory Board shall:

Render advisory opinions concerning the effectiveness of the Small Business Stationary Source Technical and Environmental Compliance Assistance Program, difficulties encountered, and degree and severity of enforcement;


Make periodic reports to the General Assembly and the Administrator of the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency concerning the compliance of the State Small Business Stationary Source Technical and Environmental Compliance Assistance Program with the requirements of the federal Paperwork Reduction Act, the federal Regulatory Flexibility Act, and the federal Equal Access to Justice Act;


Review information for small business stationary sources to ensure that such information is understandable by the layperson; and


Develop and disseminate reports and advisory opinions through the Office of Small Business Ombudsman.
